        "code": {
          "language": "plaintext",
          "showLineNumbers": false,
          "showMiniMap": false
        },
        "content": "## Interpret missing data deliberately\n\n- No traffic: a covered request/event counter exists and its increase is zero.\n- Unknown: an expected health, configuration, or event series is absent.\n- Disabled: a verified deployment setting disables the feature.\n- Partial: mixed application schemas or only some targets expose a metric.\n\n## Current limitations\n\n- Audit writer counters do not acknowledge Loki ingestion.\n- Bundle age and Retry-After gauges are last observed values.\n- Tempo environment and Prometheus namespace are mapped manually.\n- Backend discard and TSDB metrics may be platform-wide.\n\nOpen the implementation plan for required instrumentation and acceptance scenarios.",
        "mode": "markdown"
      },
      "pluginVersion": "11.0.0",
      "title": "How to Read Coverage States",
      "type": "text"
    }
